Letov Obratz was a dapper purple-skinned tiefling of old money, with small, polished obsidian horns and an incredibly complex multi-layered suit of shifting, iridescent fabrics that changed texture with his mood. He carried an expensive cane of something like obsidian, and his grandfather had built [[Org/Garrick Textiles/index|Garrick Textiles]] from the ground up.

He took his sick nephew's place on the [[Phenomena/Pilgrimage|pilgrimage]], and set about building the Org's fane aboard the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]: a marble entrance hall, a cramped bedroom, and a grand staircase that leads nowhere, the beginnings of a much larger building he ran out of energy to finish. He had brought a ton of fabric and meant to add an atelier, a runway and soirees once the place had a kitchen and running water. He was friendly and welcoming, and declined the Party's offer to move in with them, saying he had been taught not to lean on others. His ponchos, never popular in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], sold well in [[Geography/Velthara/index|Velthara]].

He died at the banquet the evening the Providence left [[Geography/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]], when the first tithe was drawn and his weak heart could not pay it; the sprite secretary who hovered about him died with him.
